From: Aurora <aurora@child-of-light-recomp.local>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 13:45:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 20] recompiler: declare __imp__ imports extern "C" in
 ppc_recomp_shared.h

Import stubs (__imp__RtlEnterCriticalSection, __imp__KeTlsAlloc, ...)
are defined by the ReXGlue runtime with C linkage (REX_EXPORT, which
expands to extern "C"). The shared header declared every symbol with
PPC_EXTERN_FUNC (plain `extern`, C++ linkage), so the linker looked
for the mangled name and failed on all 40 referenced imports
("ld.lld: error: undefined symbol: __imp__RtlEnterCriticalSection
(PPCContext&, unsigned char*) ... did you mean: extern "C"
__imp__RtlEnterCriticalSection, defined in librexruntime.so" —
Fase 2 build 7). Emit PPC_FUNC_IMPL (extern "C") for symbols whose
name starts with __imp__; regular sub_* functions keep
PPC_EXTERN_FUNC (their weak aliases resolve through the C-linkage
__imp__sub_* bodies the TUs define).

---
--- a/XenonRecomp/recompiler.cpp
+++ b/XenonRecomp/recompiler.cpp
@@ -2584,8 +2584,16 @@
         println("#include \"ppc_config.h\"");
         println("#include \"ppc_context.h\"\n");
 
+        // Import stubs are defined by the runtime with C linkage
+        // (REX_EXPORT); a C++-linkage declaration mangles the name and
+        // the link fails. Regular functions keep PPC_EXTERN_FUNC.
         for (auto& symbol : image.symbols)
-            println("PPC_EXTERN_FUNC({});", symbol.name);
+        {
+            if (symbol.name.rfind("__imp__", 0) == 0)
+                println("PPC_FUNC_IMPL({});", symbol.name);
+            else
+                println("PPC_EXTERN_FUNC({});", symbol.name);
+        }
 
         SaveCurrentOutData("ppc_recomp_shared.h");
     }
